# SUPERSEDED -- do not use.
#
# The old 71-r28s-netled.rules matched KERNEL=="wan"/"lan", the LED class names
# that only existed while the DTB carried label="wan"/"lan"; it also bound the
# LEDs by interface *name*, which is exactly what is unreliable here.
# LED binding (and the ethernet renaming) now lives in
# /etc/udev/rules.d/90-r28s-hwfix.rules -> /usr/local/sbin/r28s-hwfix.sh,
# which resolves each LED to its interface through the hardware device path.
